         # Addresses issues #10611 and #10678:\n1019 |         # When plotting scatterplots and hexbinplots in IPython\n1020 |         # inline backend the colorbar axis height tends not to\n1021 |         # exactly match the parent axis height.\n1022 |         # The difference is due to small fractional differences\n1023 |         # in floating points with similar representation.\n1024 |         # To deal with this, this method forces the colorbar\n1025 |         # height to take the height of the parent axes.\n1026 |         # For a more detailed description of the issue\n1027 |         # see the following link:\n1028 |         # https://github.com/ipython/ipython/issues/11215\n1029 | \n1030 |         # GH33389, if ax is used multiple times, we should always\n1031 |         # use the last one which contains the latest information\n1032 |         # about the ax\n1033 |         img = ax.collections[-1]\n1034 |         return self.fig.colorbar(img, ax=ax, **kwds)\n```\n\nFound file `pandas/tseries/frequencies.py`.\nFound file `pandas/core/index.py`.\nSource: Retrieved entity using keyword search (bm25).\nHint: Use more detailed query to get the full content of some if needed.\n\n\n\n##Searching for term \"dependencies requires\"...\n### Search Result:\nFound `pandas/io/gbq.py:_try_import`.\nSource: Retrieved code content using keyword search (bm25).\n```\n  1 | \"\"\" Google BigQuery support \"\"\"\n  2 | from __future__ import annotations\n  3 | \n  4 | from typing import (\n  5 |     TYPE_CHECKING,\n  6 |     Any,\n  7 | )\n  8 | \n  9 | from pandas.compat._optional import import_optional_dependency\n 10 | \n 11 | if TYPE_CHECKING:\n 12 |     from pandas import DataFrame\n 13 | \n 14 | \n 15 | def _try_import():\n 16 |     # since pandas is a dependency of pandas-gbq\n 17 |     # we need to import on first use\n 18 |     msg = (\n 19 |         \"pandas-gbq is required to load data from Google BigQuery. \"\n 20 |         \"See the docs: https://pandas-gbq.readthedoc