arning to the docstring.\n 15 | \n 16 |     The optional extra argument will be appended to the deprecation message\n 17 |     and the docstring. Note: to use this with the default value for extra, put\n 18 |     in an empty of parentheses:\n 19 | \n 20 |     Examples\n 21 |     --------\n 22 |     >>> from sklearn.utils import deprecated\n 23 |     >>> deprecated()\n 24 |     <sklearn.utils.deprecation.deprecated object at ...>\n 25 |     >>> @deprecated()\n 26 |     ... def some_function(): pass\n 27 | \n 28 |     Parameters\n 29 |     ----------\n 30 |     extra : str, default=''\n 31 |           To be added to the deprecation messages.\n 32 |     \"\"\"\n 33 | \n 34 |     # Adapted from https://wiki.python.org/moin/PythonDecoratorLibrary,\n 35 |     # but with many changes.\n 36 | \n 37 |     def __init__(self, extra=\"\"):\n 38 |         self.extra = extra\n```\nHint: \nThe code for class `sklearn/utils/deprecation.py:deprecated` is incomplete; search `sklearn/utils/deprecation.py:deprecated` for the full content if needed.\n\nFound `sklearn/utils/_pprint.py:KeyValTuple`, `sklearn/utils/_pprint.py:KeyValTuple.__repr__`, `sklearn/utils/_pprint.py:KeyValTupleParam`.\nSource: Retrieved code content using keyword search (bm25).\n```\n  1 | \"\"\"This module contains the _EstimatorPrettyPrinter class used in\n  2 | BaseEstimator.__repr__ for pretty-printing estimators\"\"\"\n  3 | \n  4 | # Authors: The scikit-learn developers\n  5 | # SPDX-License-Identifier: BSD-3-Clause\n  6 | \n  7 | # Copyright (c) 2001, 2002, 2003, 2004, 2005, 2006, 2007, 2008, 2009, 2010,\n  8 | # 2011, 2012, 2013, 2014, 2015, 2016, 2017, 2018 Python Software Foundation;\n  9 | # All Rights Reserved\n 10 | \n 11 | # Authors: Fred L. Drake, Jr. <fdrake@acm.org> (built-in CPython pprint module)\n 12 | #          Nicolas Hug (scikit-learn specific changes)\n 13 | \n 14 | # License: PSF License version 2 (see below)\n 15 | \n 16 | # PYTHON SOFTWARE FOUNDATION LICENSE VERSION 2\n 17 | # ----------